        THE BUY-SIDE NDA. Parented by Opportunity__c. Four states:
        Pending -> Sent -> Received -> Signed.

        WHY FOUR AND NOT THREE (decision D14.1, 2026-08-09). The source document describes
        Pending -> Received -> Signed, which reads as the broker-facing milestones rather than
        the full internal process. The org already ran Pending -> Sent -> Signed, with
        Date_Sent__c pairing to Sent and RecordStageAdvanceService encoding that hop. Adding
        Received rather than RENAMING Sent is what makes this change purely ADDITIVE: every
        acquisition NDA already in the org keeps a valid value, Date_Sent__c keeps the state it
        pairs with, and THERE IS NO DATA MIGRATION on this side. Received is the distinction the
        document itself draws at Part 1 lines 38 and 41 - "NDA not yet received from broker" vs
        "the NDA has been received".

        WHAT IS RESTRICTED OUT: Not Sent and Declined. Both belong to the disposition path.
        Declined in particular must never be reachable here - an acquisition NDA has no
        decline off-ramp in the document, and the Opportunity gate
        NDA_Signed_Before_Deal_Progression keys on NDA_Signed__c, which the
        NDA_Signed_Status_Sync flow derives from Status__c.

        WARNING (SUPERSEDED 2026-08-20 FOR THIS FIELD — SEE CORRECTION BELOW) - RECORD-TYPE
        PICKLIST RESTRICTION IS UI-ONLY. It is NOT enforced by Apex DML. A hand-crafted
        advanceTo(acquisitionNdaId, 'Declined') would still write, which is why
        RecordStageAdvanceService's explicit-target allow-list has to become record-type-aware
        in the same tranche. That is Apex work and lives in the parallel developer change.

        CORRECTED 2026-08-20 - THE PARAGRAPH ABOVE IS FALSE FOR THIS FIELD, MEASURED, NOT
        ASSUMED. `NDA__c.Status__c` is `<restricted>true</restricted>` (see
        objects/NDA__c/fields/Status__c.field-meta.xml). A restricted picklist's record-type
        value subset IS enforced by Apex DML, not just the UI: a test that writes
        `Status__c = 'Declined'` directly onto an Acquisition_NDA record via plain
        `update` fails at the DML layer with `INVALID_OR_NULL_FOR_RESTRICTED_PICKLIST` — see
        `NdaSignedStatusSyncTest.acquisitionNdaDeclinedViaApiResidual_isRefusedByThePicklistRestrictionItself`,
        measured on usman-dpeg (deploy 0Afiw000000Nb27CAC, test run 707iw000002YDY0AAO). The
        general "UI-only" claim is still TRUE for an UNRESTRICTED picklist — Apex can write any
        master value there regardless of record type. It is FALSE specifically because this
        field is restricted; do not generalise this correction to an unrestricted picklist, and
        do not assume it extends to any OTHER restricted picklist in this repo without its own
        measurement. Whether RecordStageAdvanceService's NDA_DISPOSITION_EXPLICIT_TARGETS
        record-type-aware split is still NECESSARY given this correction (as opposed to
        harmless-but-redundant defensive code) is a separate, unresolved question — not decided
        or acted on here; see that class's own header for the reasoning this correction now
        calls into question.

        Party_Role__c IS ENUMERATED HERE WITH NO DEFAULT, DELIBERATELY. A record type cannot
        expose an empty picklist, so both values must be listed; but Buyer/Introducing Broker
        are counterparty roles in a SALE. On an acquisition DPEG is itself the buyer, so a
        default of Buyer would silently name US - the same meaning inversion ARCHITECTURE.md
        records for Ball_In_Court__c. The field is also excluded from the acquisition layout.
        Counter_Signed_Date__c is likewise disposition-only and is a plain Date, so it needs no
        entry here at all.

        EVERY PICKLIST ON THE OBJECT IS ENUMERATED - Status__c, Method__c and Party_Role__c -
        because a record type file that omits a picklist silently drops all of its values from
        that type. Precedent: objects/Disposition__c/recordTypes/Off_Market.recordType-meta.xml.
        NDA__c has exactly three picklists after this tranche.

        No <businessProcess> - that element is for Opportunity, Case, Lead and Solution only.

        POST-DEPLOY, NOT DEPLOYABLE: this record type must be assigned in every profile in use
        (System Administrator included - Modify All Data is an OBJECT permission and confers no
        record-type access), a per-profile DEFAULT must be chosen, and the existing NDA rows
        must be migrated off Master (branch on the parent: Disposition__c populated ->
        Disposition_NDA, else Acquisition_NDA). profiles/** is .forceignore'd in this repo, so
        none of that can be deployed from here.

        =====================================================================
        AMENDED 2026-08-16 - SEQUENCE REVERSED. THE D14.1 PARAGRAPHS ABOVE DESCRIBE THE
        SUPERSEDED "Pending -> Sent -> Received -> Signed" ORDER AND ARE RETAINED VERBATIM AS
        THE RECORD OF WHAT CHANGED. THE VALUE SET ITSELF DID NOT CHANGE - still exactly Pending,
        Sent, Received, Signed - only their intended PROCESS ORDER did.
        =====================================================================

        THE SEQUENCE IS NOW Pending -> Received -> Signed -> Sent, and 'Sent' IS NOW TERMINAL,
        not 'Signed': the broker's NDA arrives (Pending), DPEG receives it (Received) and signs
        it (Signed), then DPEG sends the signed copy back to the broker (Sent). The
        <picklistValues><picklist>Status__c</picklist> block below was reordered to match, and
        the companion Path (pathAssistants/NDA_Path_Acquisition) was reordered the same way -
        see that file's own 2026-08-16 amendment for the full rationale and for the info-text
        wording that still describes the old direction and needs a separate reviewed reword.

        ⚠ WHETHER THIS LIST ORDER ACTUALLY CONTROLS THE RUNTIME Status__c DROPDOWN ORDER FOR
        THIS RECORD TYPE, INDEPENDENTLY OF THE MASTER FIELD'S OWN VALUE ORDER, WAS NOT VERIFIED
        AS PART OF THIS CHANGE - see the companion Path file's amendment, which flags the same
        open question for the Path's own step order. The master Status__c field
        (objects/NDA__c/fields/Status__c.field-meta.xml) was deliberately NOT touched here.

        CORRECTED 2026-08-16 - the paragraph this replaces asserted that the NDA_Signed_Status_Sync
        flow "was made record-type-aware in the same change: Acquisition_NDA now reads 'Signed' OR
        'Sent' as signed". THAT IS FALSE. The flow was never touched by this change - git history
        shows it last modified in an earlier commit, it contains zero record-type branching, and
        it tests Status__c = 'Signed' only. No flow change was needed, and none was made.

        WHY NO FLOW CHANGE WAS NEEDED, VERIFIED BY MECHANISM RATHER THAN BY TRUSTING THE FLOW'S
        OWN DESCRIPTION: NDA_Signed_Status_Sync's Is_Signed decision sets NDA_Signed__c TRUE when
        Status__c = 'Signed', and its false branch carries a
        <defaultConnectorLabel>Not Signed</defaultConnectorLabel> but NO <defaultConnector> -
        nothing connects to the flow's own Set_Signed_False assignment, so that assignment is
        UNREACHABLE. The checkbox therefore LATCHES: once true it stays true through every later
        Status__c change, including this reorder's new final hop from 'Signed' to 'Sent'. Moving
        an acquisition NDA off 'Signed' and onto the new terminal 'Sent' therefore leaves
        NDA_Signed__c TRUE and the Opportunity gate NDA_Signed_Before_Deal_Progression unaffected -
        no widening of the flow's logic was required to make that true, because the flow already
        never turns the checkbox back off. See flows/NDA_Signed_Status_Sync's own 2026-08-16
        comment for the full rationale and the warning against ever connecting that dead branch;
        RecordStageAdvanceService's class header carries the same analysis - the two are written
        to agree, not to be read independently.

        TWO FURTHER KNOWN CONSEQUENCES OF THE REORDER, DOCUMENTED HERE AND DELIBERATELY NOT FIXED
        AS PART OF THIS CHANGE - both need a USER decision, not a metadata edit:

        (a) NDA__c.Days_Out__c (IF(ISBLANK(Date_Sent__c), null, TODAY() - Date_Sent__c)) now
        measures the wrong thing for an acquisition NDA. Under the old order 'Sent' was a middle
        step, so this counted days an NDA had been out awaiting signature. Under this order 'Sent'
        is TERMINAL, so the counter starts when the NDA is FINISHED and grows forever afterward.
        It is user-visible: Days_Out__c is a column on reports/Acquisitions/NDA_Tracker_Recent, so
        a completed NDA will read "out 340 days". See the field's own XML comment
        (objects/NDA__c/fields/Days_Out__c.field-meta.xml) for the candidate remedies. The formula
        was deliberately NOT changed here.

        (b) SUPERSEDED 2026-08-16 (SAME-DAY FOLLOW-UP) - THE PARAGRAPH THIS REPLACES GUESSED WRONG
        ABOUT WHAT THE LABEL WAS, AND THE ACTUAL LABEL WAS MORE DANGEROUS THAN THE GUESS. It read
        "OpportunityDocStatusController exposes ndaSent = nda.Date_Sent__c and the component
        labels it as the NDA being sent to the counterparty" and reasoned from the DTO member's
        name rather than from the component itself. THAT IS FALSE. The live lwc/dealDocStatus
        label was `Received <date>`, not "sent to the counterparty" - confirmed by a developer
        agent actually reading the component, not inferred from the DTO name.

        WHY THE REAL LABEL WAS MORE DANGEROUS THAN THE GUESSED ONE. The guessed label ("sent to
        the counterparty") would have merely contradicted the new order - a user could notice the
        mismatch and go looking for why. The ACTUAL label, "Received <date>", did something worse:
        this same reorder made 'Received' a genuine step in the acquisition sequence with its own
        field (NDA__c.Date_Received__c, added in this same follow-up - see that field's own
        comment). So the stale label did not read as WRONG, it read as a CORRECT date for a
        DIFFERENT step - a user seeing "Received Mar 10" would reasonably conclude that is when
        the broker's NDA arrived, when it is in fact when DPEG returned the signed copy. A
        misleading-but-plausible label is worse than an obviously wrong one, because nothing
        prompts anyone to check it.

        FIXED, SAME FOLLOW-UP: the label now reads `Signed copy returned <date>`, and the DTO
        member on OpportunityDocStatusController was RENAMED ndaSent -> ndaSignedCopyReturned.
        Anyone grepping for ndaSent after 2026-08-16 will find nothing - the new name is recorded
        here for exactly that reason. Apex/LWC were out of scope for the metadata-only NDA
        tranche this file otherwise belongs to; this fix landed in the parallel developer change.

        TWO FURTHER, OPEN CONSEQUENCES OF THE SAME REORDER, RECORDED HERE BRIEFLY BECAUSE THEY
        CURRENTLY LIVE ONLY IN AN AGENT REPORT:

        - NDA_TONE in lwc/dealDocStatus may now be INVERTED. 'Sent' renders blue (in progress)
          though it is now terminal, while 'Signed' renders green (done) though it is now
          mid-sequence. 'Received: blue' was added because that status was falling through to
          grey, the unknown-status fallback. The Sent/Signed colours were deliberately NOT changed
          as part of this fix - it is a real judgement call (the deal gate releases at Signed; the
          NDA process itself finishes at Sent) and is left with the user.

        - A DATA RESIDUAL THE REORDER CANNOT FIX. The value set was reordered, not migrated, so
          acquisition NDAs worked before 2026-08-16 carry Date_Sent__c stamped under the OLD
          meaning ("we sent it out"), and nothing on the record distinguishes those rows from ones
          stamped under the new meaning. The label above is therefore UNCONDITIONAL by necessity -
          a status-conditional label would invent a rule the data cannot support.

        =====================================================================
        AMENDED 2026-08-27 - 'Sent' REMOVED FROM THIS RECORD TYPE, BY USER DECISION. EVERYTHING
        ABOVE THIS BLOCK ABOUT A FOUR-STATE Pending/Received/Signed/Sent SEQUENCE, IN EITHER
        ORDER, IS NOW HISTORICAL - RETAINED VERBATIM AS THE RECORD OF WHAT CHANGED, NOT AS
        CURRENT BEHAVIOUR.
        =====================================================================

        THE ACQUISITION_NDA <picklistValues><picklist>Status__c</picklist> BLOCK BELOW NOW LISTS
        EXACTLY THREE VALUES - Pending, Received, Signed - IN THAT ORDER. 'Signed' IS NOW THE
