        measured on this exact field, a restricted picklist's record-type subset IS enforced by
        Apex DML, not just the UI, so that write throws
        `INVALID_OR_NULL_FOR_RESTRICTED_PICKLIST` rather than silently succeeding or silently
        failing open. The org's one live acquisition NDA was sitting at 'Signed' when this was
        found, so the broken button was on screen.

        WHAT THIS EDIT DOES NOT DO: it does not touch the master Status__c field's value list
        (objects/NDA__c/fields/Status__c.field-meta.xml) - 'Sent' remains a valid master value,
        still used by Disposition_NDA. It also does not touch
        quickActions/NDA__c.Move_to_Sent.quickAction-meta.xml, which the disposition path still
        uses. See flexipages/NDA_Record_Page's own 2026-08-27 amendment for removal of the
        acquisition-side Move_to_Sent page entry, and pathAssistants/NDA_Path_Acquisition's own
        2026-08-27 amendment for removal of the Sent path step - both companion edits made in the
        same corrective change, for the same reason.

        WHAT THIS EDIT LEAVES OPEN, FOR THE PARALLEL DEVELOPER STREAM, NOT DECIDED HERE:
        RecordStageAdvanceService / NDA_ACQUISITION_NEXT_STAGE's 'Signed' => 'Sent' hop is Apex
        and is out of scope for this metadata-only file; see this task's own instructions for the
        explicit carve-out. NDA__c.Days_Out__c's known mismeasurement (documented above at the
        2026-08-16 amendment, paragraph (a)) is NOT resolved by this edit either - Date_Sent__c on
        an acquisition NDA now again means "not applicable" for any row that never passed through
        the old order, which is arguably a partial return to the pre-2026-08-16 meaning, but no
        formula change was made here and none should be inferred from this comment.
